('P2425-0000045', 'myk-filler-powdersilver-shadow-075kg', 'Myk Filler Powder#Silver shadow - 0.75kg', 'Simple', NULL, 'a:1:{i:0;s:14:\"SG2024-0000003\";}', 'https://youtu.be/NEU8XSzZPhY?si=fUlkyU_VWaZ9ICtR', 'uploads/master/product/products/P2425-0000045/c6c2173335f9c4b06308b10e2b0183c3.pdf', '3214', 'PC2024-0000008', 'PSC2425-0000019', 'UOM2023-0000004', 0, 0, 'N;', 'Include', 'TX2023-0000002', 650, 350, 'auto', '<p><strong>Myk Epoxy Resin 1.25kg</strong> is a high-performance epoxy resin system designed for a variety of construction and repair applications. Here&rsquo;s a detailed description:</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Product Overview:</strong></h3>\n\n<p>Myk Epoxy Resin 1.25kg is a two-component epoxy system that provides strong adhesion, durability, and a smooth finish. It is suitable for industrial, commercial, and residential use, offering versatility and reliability in various applications.</p>\n\n<h3><strong>Key Features:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>High Adhesion:</strong> Provides excellent bonding to a wide range of substrates, including concrete, metal, wood, and masonry.</li>\n	<li><strong>Durability:</strong> Resists mechanical stress, chemicals, and environmental factors, ensuring long-lasting performance even in harsh conditions.</li>\n	<li><strong>Versatile Application:</strong> Can be used for bonding, sealing, coating, and repairing tasks, making it a flexible solution for different needs.</li>\n	<li><strong>Smooth Finish:</strong> After curing, the resin delivers a smooth, even surface that can be sanded and painted if required.</li>\n	<li><strong>Ease of Use:</strong> The two components are easy to mix and apply, with manageable curing times for practical use.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Applications:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Bonding:</strong> Ideal for joining materials where a strong, reliable bond is required, such as metal to concrete or wood to masonry.</li>\n	<li><strong>Sealing:</strong> Effective for sealing gaps, cracks, and joints to prevent water ingress and protect surfaces from damage.</li>\n	<li><strong>Coating:</strong> Suitable for applying protective coatings on floors, walls, and other surfaces to enhance durability and resistance to wear.</li>\n	<li><strong>Repair:</strong> Used for repairing damaged surfaces, filling voids, and reinforcing structural elements.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></h3>\n\n<ol>\n	<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Ensure surfaces are clean, dry, and free of contaminants such as dust, oil, or grease.</li>\n	<li><strong>Mixing:</strong> Combine the epoxy resin and hardener in the specified ratio provided by the manufacturer. Mix thoroughly until a uniform consistency is achieved.</li>\n	<li><strong>Application:</strong> Apply the mixed resin to the prepared surface using appropriate tools, such as a brush, roller, or trowel, depending on the application.</li>\n	<li><strong>Curing:</strong> Allow the resin to cure fully as per the product&rsquo;s specifications. Curing times may vary based on temperature, humidity, and other environmental conditions.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3><strong>Storage:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Conditions:</strong> Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight and moisture.</li>\n	<li><strong>Packaging:</strong> Keep containers tightly sealed when not in use to prevent contamination and premature curing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Safety:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Precautions:</strong> Follow standard safety practices, including wearing protective gloves, goggles, and ensuring adequate ventilation during application.</li>\n	<li><strong>Handling:</strong> Avoid contact with skin and eyes. In case of accidental contact, rinse thoroughly with water and seek medical attention if necessary.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><strong>Technical Specifications:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Packaging Size:</strong> 1.25kg</li>\n	<li><strong>Component Ratio:</strong> As per manufacturer&rsquo;s instructio